{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>The sons of the Elohim.</b> Rabbi Shimon bar Yochai called them sons of judges, and he cursed those who call them sons of Elohim. And why did Scripture call them sons of Elohim? Rabbi Yochanan and Resh Lakish said: because they multiplied without toil and without suffering." "<b>For they are good.</b> Fair." "<b>Of all that they chose.</b> They were learned in supernal wisdom and chose for themselves wives similar to them in their traits, to sire mighty ones like themselves from them, and took them by force; and therefore they angered the Holy One, blessed be He."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:07.610864969Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}